node_modules/
dist/

# WI-4419 (2026-07-12): agent state dirs (.papercusp/) appear inside submodules too,
# and git-sync auto-commits the superproject AND every submodule — so any scratch a
# gitignore does not cover is committed automatically and then swept into every
# release bundle by the sidecar source-tar glob. The superproject .gitignore does NOT
# reach inside a submodule, so the guard must be repeated here. Depth-matching (**/)
# on purpose: a slash-bearing pattern is anchored to THIS file's directory.
.papercusp/scratch/
.papercusp/vitest-tmp/
.papercusp/tmp/
.papercusp/tmp-*/
.papercusp/logs/
.papercusp/bench-reports/
.papercusp/pi-sessions/
**/.papercusp/scratch/
**/.papercusp/vitest-tmp/
**/.papercusp/tmp/
**/.papercusp/tmp-*/
**/.papercusp/logs/
**/.papercusp/bench-reports/
**/.papercusp/pi-sessions/

# WI-761481 (2026-08-29): the SAME submodule-reach gap as above, for the Vite/Vitest
# cache dir. `defineVitestConfig` sets `cacheDir: '.vitest-tmp'` (a deliberate local
# path — TMPDIR is read-only on the dev box), so every workspace using the shared
# config writes .vitest-tmp/ at ITS OWN root. The superproject ignores that path, but
# that does not reach inside a submodule, and the WI-4419 block above only covers
# .papercusp/* — so .vitest-tmp/vitest/<hash>/results.json got COMMITTED in 7 generic
# submodules. That file records a per-run `duration`, so it changes on EVERY test run;
# because it is tracked, it lands in the affected-tests dependency closure and flips
# the passing-task verdict fingerprint every run. Measured: the cross-run reuse cache
# could NEVER hit (`reason=cross-run:dependency-closure-changed`, hits=0). Keep both
# forms: a slash-bearing pattern is anchored to THIS file's directory.
.vitest-tmp/
**/.vitest-tmp/

# Coverage reports — any Vitest/cargo-llvm-cov --coverage run.
#
# The SUPERPROJECT .gitignore already carries this exact rule set, but a
# superproject ignore does NOT govern inside a submodule: `git check-ignore`
# run from the repo root answers "is in submodule <p>" and declines, so the
# rule silently stops at this boundary. Without a copy HERE, git-sync (which
# commits the superproject AND every submodule) sweeps the generated report
# into this repo. Same class as EI-22195215129102176 (74 files / +54,104
# lines swept) and EI-22201289307647151 (this rule was missing from 22 of 38
# coverage-capable submodules until then).
coverage/
coverage-*/
**/coverage/
**/coverage-*/
